{title: I Know Who Holds Tomorrow}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
I don't [G]know[**] about to[G7]morrow[**], I just [C]live[**] from day to [G]day[**]
I don't [C]borrow[**] from its [G]sunshine[**] for its [A7]skies[**] may turn to [D]grey[**]
I don't [G]worry[**] o'er the [G7]future[**] for I [C]know[**] what Jesus [G]said[**]
And to[C]day[**] I'll walk be[G]side Him[**] for He [D]knows[**] what is a[G]head[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Many [C]things[**] about to[G]morrow[**], I don't [A7]seem[**] to under[D]stand[**]
But I [G]know[**] who holds to[C]morrow[**], and I [D]know[**] who holds my [G]hand[**].
